NAME
       realpath - print a resolved absolute name

SYNOPSIS
       realpath [-e | -m] [-s] [-q] [-z] [--relative-to=DIR]
          [--relative-base=DIR] FILE...

DESCRIPTION
       Makes each name absolute, removes . and .. and repeated
       slashes, and follows symbolic links (unless -s). By
       default every component but the last must exist; -e
       requires all of them, -m none.

SEE ALSO
       sh(1)

